        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219-a1">

                <pb facs="0554" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg468"/>

                <head>A.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The council of the secretaries of state to the
                        citizens chosen as representatives who met yesterday in the hall affected to
                        the national representation.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Port
                                au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3,
                        1873</date>.<lb/>(70th year of independence.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: As the senate for want of one member
                    to make up its constitutional majority of twenty, that is to say, two-thirds of
                    the thirty members composing this grand body, could not organize last week, so
                    the chamber of representatives should await the majority of its members,
                    demanded by the combined requirements of the 84th and 51st articles of the
                    constitution, before organizing or taking any action capable of receiving the
                    sanction of the executive power.</p>
                <p>It is the duty of us all to respect the fundamental law, and it is to conjure to
                    this end that we send to you the expression of our very high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>
                                NISSAGE SAGET.
                            </item>
                            <item>S. LIAUTAUD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Secretary of War, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></item>
                            <item>DAMIEN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary
                                    of Interior, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></item>
                            <item>L. ÉTHEART,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Secretary of Finance, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></item>
                            <item>O. RAMEAU,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Secretary of Justice, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
